1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:03,500
Stay close to fellow fairies,
namely me.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:05,080
Since we're precious stones,

3
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:06,960
we two have
a great deal in common.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,710
Is that so?

5
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:10,420
I don't find us alike at all.

6
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:13,130
You're quite vigilant.

7
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:16,330
If you weren't,
you wouldn't survive for long.

8
00:00:22,710 --> 00:00:24,330
From opal.

9
00:01:55,330 --> 00:01:57,460
[birds chirp]

10
00:01:57,540 --> 00:02:00,040
Comrades,
I'm glad to see you're all here!

11
00:02:00,130 --> 00:02:01,670
What's this nonsense?

12
00:02:01,750 --> 00:02:03,750
You're supposed to be helping
the artisans work.

13
00:02:03,830 --> 00:02:05,290
[MITHRIL]
Excellent point!

14
00:02:05,380 --> 00:02:07,420
For you see,
it is those very artisans

15
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:09,710
who are in desperate need
of rescue!

16
00:02:09,790 --> 00:02:10,960
Why, you ask?

17
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:12,710
Because an evil ghost is lurking

18
00:02:12,790 --> 00:02:14,420
within Holly Leaf Castle
as we speak!

19
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:15,790
[DAANA, HAL]
Huh?

20
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,290
- [sighs]
- [MITHRIL] But take heart!

21
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:20,330
Your lives are in my tiny
yet capable hands!

22
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:23,130
I'm forming a brigade
of ghost-hunting vigilantes!

23
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:25,580
We shall rout
that spirit forthwith!

24
00:02:26,790 --> 00:02:28,330
[GLADUS]
Intriguing.

25
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:29,290
[gasps]

26
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:32,290
Please include me
in this brave endeavor.

27
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,790
[MITHRIL] Your name is Gladus,
right soldier?

28
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:38,170
[GLADUS] At your service,
Captain Mithril Lid Pod.

29
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:41,000
[MITHRIL] Oh, I wholeheartedly
accept your aid!

30
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:42,380
Huh?

31
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:44,460
You can't leave yet,
Challe fenn Challe!

32
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:46,540
We're going on a patrol!

33
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:48,500
- [CHALLE] I'll be in my room.
- [gasps]

34
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:49,710
Wait, don't go!

35
00:02:49,790 --> 00:02:50,460
Without your help,

36
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:52,710
who's going to battle
the spirit to the death!

37
00:02:52,790 --> 00:02:54,540
- That's your job, Captain.
- [grunts]

38
00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:56,000
- [thuds]
- [groans]

39
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:56,920
- [stabs]
- [gasps]

40
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,500
[MITHRIL]
Oh, come on!

41
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:03,710
[exhales]

42
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:06,500
[scoffs]

43
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:08,960
[crickets chirp]

44
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,920
[ANNE]
I'll just put this away.

45
00:03:14,330 --> 00:03:15,750
There.

46
00:03:15,830 --> 00:03:17,290
That's enough for now.

47
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:18,630
Great work, everyone!

48
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:20,420
[ALL sigh]

49
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:26,880
[ANNE] Oh, right.
Mithril isn't sleeping in here.

50
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,380
He said he was ghost hunting.

51
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:30,580
Hmm.

52
00:03:36,210 --> 00:03:38,080
I'm so tired.

53
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:41,290
- [door slams]
- [gasps]

54
00:03:42,170 --> 00:03:43,880
- Beside you!
- Huh?

55
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,250
What, Challe?

56
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,920
Huh?

57
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,330
- [screams]
- [gasps]

58
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:51,670
Put on the lamp!

59
00:03:51,750 --> 00:03:54,210
- [yells] What's happening?
- [boy] Stop that!

60
00:03:54,290 --> 00:03:58,210
- [CHALLE] Do it now!
- [boy grunts] Let go of me!

61
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:00,960
[man grunts]

62
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,500
[ANNE]
Who is that?

63
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:04,080
- [CHALLE] The ghost.
- [ANNE] Ghost?

64
00:04:04,170 --> 00:04:06,250
I am not a ghost, you fool!

65
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:08,170
Uh...

66
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:12,960
Oh no, he's dead!

67
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,460
Or is he?

68
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:16,920
I'm not sure
whether ghosts can die!

69
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
He fainted, that's all.

70
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:23,420
[ANNE]
Um, excuse me.

71
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,080
- [screams]
- I tricked you!

72
00:04:25,170 --> 00:04:26,880
Oh, you poor idiots!

73
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:29,330
That's what you get
for letting me go!

74
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,670
[boy groans]

75
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:33,040
[gasps] What's wrong now!

76
00:04:33,630 --> 00:04:35,170
Oh, Master.

77
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:37,000
I'm so sorry.

78
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:39,710
Who's his Master?

79
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,830
[ELLIOTT]
So, this is the big scary ghost

80
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:43,920
we've been hearing about?

81
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,790
[MITHRIL]
He's the root of the mystery?

82
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:48,790
[CHALLE]
All the footprints were his.

83
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:52,380
I'd say he's a fairy
who can pass through objects.

84
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:55,000
[ANNE] That explains
what happened to the locks.

85
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,960
[CHALLE] Last night,
he was on the first floor

86
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,830
playing tricks on the artisans,

87
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,540
so tonight,
I thought it'd be wise

88
00:05:01,630 --> 00:05:03,630
to lie in wait for him
on the second floor.

89
00:05:03,710 --> 00:05:04,880
[ANNE]
And what we thought was a ghost

90
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:06,790
turned out to be a young boy.

91
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:09,460
Huh?

92
00:05:09,540 --> 00:05:10,540
[gasps]

93
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:11,790
We won't hurt you!

94
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:12,710
You're safe!

95
00:05:12,790 --> 00:05:14,290
Would you tell us your name?

96
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:16,500
[boy]
I have no name to give a thief!

97
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:19,330
Thief!
You can't be referring to me!

98
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:20,250
[boy]
I am!

99
00:05:20,330 --> 00:05:23,000
Just you wait,
I'll dispose of all of you!

100
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:25,630
Hey, I'm not letting you
talk to Anne that way!

101
00:05:25,710 --> 00:05:26,920
I will have you know

102
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,250
the kingdom's religion gave us
explicit permission

103
00:05:29,330 --> 00:05:30,460
to use this place.

104
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:33,580
So, the one who shouldn't
be here is probably you.

105
00:05:33,670 --> 00:05:35,080
The church allowed you to stay?

106
00:05:35,170 --> 00:05:36,330
What's that matter?

107
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:37,960
This castle belongs

108
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:39,540
to Lord Stewart's
younger brother.

109
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:41,250
Lord Herbert of House Chamber!

110
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,330
Does that make you...

111
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:44,460
I am Noah!

112
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:47,210
The devoted page
to Lord Herbert himself.

113
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:48,830
And his orders to me were clear!

114
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:51,380
I have been charged
with guarding his castle!

115
00:05:51,830 --> 00:05:52,670
I see.

116
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:54,330
You said your name was Noah?

117
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:56,250
- That's right!
- The House Chamber?

118
00:05:56,330 --> 00:06:00,170
But don't you know they were
cast out 15 years ago?

119
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:02,130
I mean,
this Lord Herbert person

120
00:06:02,210 --> 00:06:05,080
is probably long dead by now.
- Don't you dare say he's dead!

121
00:06:05,170 --> 00:06:06,710
[groans]

122
00:06:06,790 --> 00:06:09,170
[NOAH] I know Lord Herbert is
coming home!

123
00:06:09,250 --> 00:06:11,630
No matter how many years
it takes!

124
00:06:11,710 --> 00:06:13,460
That's why I have
a responsibility

125
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,330
- to protect this castle!
- Hmm.

126
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:19,630
Sometime after your master
had departed,

127
00:06:19,710 --> 00:06:23,290
your castle had been invaded
by Millsland troops, correct?

128
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:26,210
You're just a fairy who is
being controlled by a thief!

129
00:06:26,290 --> 00:06:27,880
You'll never understand!

130
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:28,880
[gasps]

131
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,960
♪

132
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,290
It can't be!

133
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:39,130
We're travelling with this girl
because we choose to.

134
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,830
Now answer me,

135
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:45,500
Millsland soldiers came here,
isn't that right?

136
00:06:46,830 --> 00:06:47,750
[NOAH]
Yes.

137
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:51,170
They rushed in
wearing filthy armor

138
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:52,670
destroying everything.

139
00:06:53,210 --> 00:06:56,040
They ripped down
the crest of House Chamber,

140
00:06:56,130 --> 00:06:58,000
shredded the portraits.

141
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:59,580
Any furniture
that bore the crest

142
00:06:59,670 --> 00:07:01,080
was burned in the garden.

143
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:02,830
In the war,

144
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:05,830
did you think the royal family
defeated House Chamber?

145
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,290
What was the ending?

146
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:12,830
[NOAH] I thought that
House Chamber lost the war.

147
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:13,750
[ANNE]
Noah.

148
00:07:13,830 --> 00:07:15,580
[ELLIOTT]
So, do you understand now?

149
00:07:15,670 --> 00:07:18,920
The Millsland royal family
annexed this castle we're in.

150
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,080
In the end, it was donated

151
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:22,210
to the Church
of Saint Lewiston Bell.

152
00:07:22,710 --> 00:07:24,710
And we're borrowing it
from the church.

153
00:07:24,790 --> 00:07:26,130
That's why we're here.

154
00:07:26,210 --> 00:07:28,420
I think you'll agree,
that hardly makes us thieves.

155
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:29,830
Well, even so,

156
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:32,250
I know it
as Lord Herbert's castle

157
00:07:32,330 --> 00:07:34,710
and I have to protect it
until he returns.

158
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:37,210
That's what he asked of me,
and I won't disobey him.

159
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:40,040
But I just told you,
he's never coming back!

160
00:07:40,130 --> 00:07:41,290
The man's as dead
as dead can be.

161
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:42,790
Stop saying that he's dead!

162
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:44,000
[groans]

163
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:45,750
I refuse to trust anyone
who assumes

164
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:47,960
that my master is dead
without any proof at all!

165
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:49,380
You're lying!

166
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:50,540
And I won't--

167
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:52,250
[grunts]

168
00:07:52,330 --> 00:07:54,630
- [falling]
- [ANNE] Got you!

169
00:07:55,420 --> 00:07:57,040
I'll make you pay.

170
00:07:57,130 --> 00:07:58,330
I swear.

171
00:07:58,420 --> 00:07:59,790
You're weak.

172
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:01,420
You're not eating, are you?

173
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,790
Hmm.

174
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:06,630
[birds chirp]

175
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,540
Hmm.

176
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:15,000
[ANNE]
Noah, please eat, just a bit.

177
00:08:16,130 --> 00:08:18,580
[NOAH] If I want to stay here,
I can't eat anything

178
00:08:18,670 --> 00:08:21,330
except what Lord Herbert gave
to me.

179
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,790
It was an order from my master.

180
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:29,500
[ANNE] He's only allowed to eat
what Lord Herbert gave him?

181
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:32,540
How could someone give
that order?

182
00:08:33,710 --> 00:08:35,670
- [GLADUS] Anne, good morning.
- Huh?

183
00:08:35,750 --> 00:08:38,380
Oh. Hello there.

184
00:08:40,330 --> 00:08:42,710
How is the fairy
you discovered last night?

185
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:44,000
I mean, I--

186
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,460
Not well? What a shame.

187
00:08:50,170 --> 00:08:51,000
[gasps]

188
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,790
What are--

189
00:08:54,210 --> 00:08:55,790
A lovely aroma.

190
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:57,830
You smell of silver sugar.

191
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:58,750
Of course.

192
00:08:58,830 --> 00:09:01,210
I think all the artisans here
carry that smell.

193
00:09:01,670 --> 00:09:03,170
Most likely.

194
00:09:06,710 --> 00:09:11,460
But yours,
is uniquely spectacular.

195
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,630
Um, well,

196
00:09:14,710 --> 00:09:15,880
I should go!

197
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,420
There's work to do!

198
00:09:21,130 --> 00:09:22,920
She's an adorable girl.

199
00:09:23,250 --> 00:09:25,420
And she smells wonderful.

200
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,130
Don't you agree, Challe?

201
00:09:27,210 --> 00:09:30,040
That scarecrow, adorable?

202
00:09:30,130 --> 00:09:31,580
You've got odd taste.

203
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:35,040
You mean you don't
find her cute in the slightest?

204
00:09:35,790 --> 00:09:37,250
[CHALLE]
No.

205
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:39,330
I see.

206
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:42,250
And yet she's the reason that
you're here, isn't that right?

207
00:09:42,330 --> 00:09:44,830
You stay with her
because she's so dear

208
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:47,250
that you can't bear
to leave her side.

209
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:50,210
What a naive manner of thinking.

210
00:09:50,290 --> 00:09:53,170
You never show
your feelings, do you?

211
00:09:53,250 --> 00:09:55,920
You and I
are of the same origin.

212
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:00,080
So then, is it safe to assume
that we think in the same way?

213
00:10:00,170 --> 00:10:02,250
I have no interest
in how you think.

214
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:05,630
Whether you take
any interest in it or not,

215
00:10:05,710 --> 00:10:08,420
the fact is that you and I
are extremely close.

216
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:10,420
Our destinies
are bound together.

217
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:14,130
If that's your idea of a joke,
I'm not laughing.

218
00:10:15,170 --> 00:10:17,170
Picture a darkened chapel.

219
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,040
There's a hole through one wall

220
00:10:21,130 --> 00:10:24,460
and an altar positioned
at the very back.

221
00:10:25,210 --> 00:10:28,170
There once were ornaments
adorning the entrance

222
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:30,330
but now the ceiling
and walls are scarred

223
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:32,080
with the signs of excavation.

224
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,880
How do you know that place?

225
00:10:34,290 --> 00:10:37,170
It's exactly as I suspected.

226
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:39,500
If you'd show me
even the slightest hint

227
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:41,420
of your sincere feelings,

228
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:44,040
I'd happily tell you everything.

229
00:10:44,630 --> 00:10:47,130
[CHALLE]
What? How does he know?

230
00:10:50,630 --> 00:10:52,460
Who is he?

231
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:54,920
[GLEN]
Noah, did you say?

232
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,420
I'm worried that he might
starve himself to death.

233
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,830
[ANNE]
So am I.

234
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:00,710
He says
if he wants to stay here,

235
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:02,040
he's only allowed
to eat the food

236
00:11:02,130 --> 00:11:03,880
that his master gave him

237
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,130
but I don't understand

238
00:11:05,210 --> 00:11:07,330
why he doesn't just run away
and be free.

239
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:09,460
I assume it means
that his master left

240
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:12,040
- with Noah's wing in hand.
- [ANNE] Oh.

241
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:13,670
[GLEN]
The poor thing.

242
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:15,710
No wonder he keeps waiting
for a master

243
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:18,040
who will never return.

244
00:11:18,130 --> 00:11:20,880
[ANNE] I see,
so that's why he won't leave.

245
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:23,290
Fairies desire
sugar confections.

246
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:25,710
Perhaps you could persuade him
to eat one of those.

247
00:11:25,790 --> 00:11:27,460
Oh, you're right.

248
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:28,920
Then I'll try that!

249
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[birds chirp]

250
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:38,290
I wonder if he's still awake.

251
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:39,210
Let's see.

252
00:11:40,460 --> 00:11:41,290
Huh?

253
00:11:43,330 --> 00:11:44,790
♪

254
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:46,210
- [ANNE] Noah?
- Huh?

255
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:49,920
- [NOAH] Oh, it's just the thief.
- [ANNE] What are you doing?

256
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:52,880
[ANNE]
This must be Lord Herbert.

257
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:54,420
Right.

258
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:56,790
That explains why
this one painting isn't dirty

259
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:58,380
like the rest of them.

260
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:01,670
Tell me.

261
00:12:01,750 --> 00:12:03,540
Did Lord Herbert take your wing
with him

262
00:12:03,630 --> 00:12:05,880
on the day
he departed the castle?

263
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:08,080
Of course not,
he's not a bad person!

264
00:12:08,170 --> 00:12:10,380
He gave it back to me
before he left home!

265
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:12,460
What?
He didn't take it?

266
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:13,540
That's right!

267
00:12:13,630 --> 00:12:16,290
[ANNE] Then why have you
stayed here for 15 years?

268
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:18,170
If you have your wing,
then you're free.

269
00:12:18,250 --> 00:12:19,380
Are you dense?

270
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:21,080
As I've already told you,

271
00:12:21,170 --> 00:12:23,790
I take Lord Herbert's wishes
very seriously

272
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:26,420
and I was the one ordered
to take care of the castle.

273
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:29,000
You're sure?
That's exactly what he told you?

274
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:31,250
Protect the castle, never leave,

275
00:12:31,330 --> 00:12:33,630
and don't eat anything
that he didn't give to you?

276
00:12:33,710 --> 00:12:35,830
[gasps] Well, I...

277
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:37,750
I just want to keep my word.

278
00:12:37,830 --> 00:12:40,630
He said he wouldn't take me
with him into battle

279
00:12:40,710 --> 00:12:43,130
and that I should look after
the castle while he's away.

280
00:12:43,210 --> 00:12:45,330
Lord Herbert said it's something
only I could do.

281
00:12:47,130 --> 00:12:48,250
But he also said

282
00:12:48,330 --> 00:12:50,710
that once I've eaten
all the sugar confections,

283
00:12:50,790 --> 00:12:52,080
- I should leave.
- [gasps]

284
00:12:52,170 --> 00:12:53,290
If I ate anything else,

285
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:55,830
I wouldn't be allowed
to stay any longer.

286
00:12:56,830 --> 00:12:58,210
[ANNE]
Wait a minute.

287
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:00,170
I see now.

288
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,880
He wanted him to run away.

289
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:06,210
So, Noah, did you eat
the sugar confections?

290
00:13:06,290 --> 00:13:07,540
Only some!

291
00:13:07,630 --> 00:13:09,130
But I left one final piece!

292
00:13:09,210 --> 00:13:12,080
And that means I don't have
to leave the castle just yet!

293
00:13:12,170 --> 00:13:14,040
I'll wait for Lord Herbert!

294
00:13:14,790 --> 00:13:16,210
Noah...

295
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:20,710
That's a...

296
00:13:20,790 --> 00:13:23,420
[ANNE] It's one of the snow
crystals we're making.

297
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:25,420
I asked if we could spare one.

298
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:27,670
I was hoping you'd eat it.

299
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:31,040
After all, I'm sure Lord Herbert
would prefer

300
00:13:31,130 --> 00:13:34,920
that you were healthy
while waiting for him, so...

301
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,540
[NOAH]
I can't.

302
00:13:36,630 --> 00:13:38,880
If I disobey, then I have
to leave the castle.

303
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:43,040
I'm sorry,
but I'm Lord Herbert's page.

304
00:13:43,130 --> 00:13:45,540
- There's no choice.
- [ANNE] Noah.

305
00:13:48,210 --> 00:13:49,290
[CHALLE]
How?

306
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,380
There's no reason he should be
talking about a place

307
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:54,000
that only Liz and I knew.

308
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:58,880
Unless...

309
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,080
- [thuds]
- [gasps]

310
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:04,210
[CHALLE]
What are you doing?

311
00:14:04,290 --> 00:14:06,460
Oh, you're here.

312
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:08,540
♪

313
00:14:11,630 --> 00:14:13,080
Thanks for your help.

314
00:14:13,170 --> 00:14:14,920
Noah couldn't stand anymore.

315
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,170
I assumed he was light enough
to carry on my own.

316
00:14:18,250 --> 00:14:19,960
- Is that for him?
- Mmm-hmm.

317
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:22,130
But he still wouldn't eat it.

318
00:14:22,210 --> 00:14:25,250
And he told me that his master
gave him his wing back.

319
00:14:25,330 --> 00:14:26,170
[CHALLE]
Oh?

320
00:14:26,250 --> 00:14:27,580
[ANNE]
Mmm-hmm.

321
00:14:27,670 --> 00:14:31,630
I think Lord Herbert must've
wanted him to leave this place.

322
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:35,040
That's the real reason
why he gave that order

323
00:14:35,130 --> 00:14:36,830
but because of the promise
they made,

324
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:39,630
Noah's still waiting for him.

325
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:43,290
- You're a silver sugar master.
- Huh?

326
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:47,630
So, make something
that he likes,

327
00:14:47,710 --> 00:14:49,880
something that he can
be convinced to eat.

328
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:51,630
You think I can?

329
00:14:52,170 --> 00:14:53,460
You think I'm wrong?

330
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:56,250
No, you're not wrong.

331
00:14:56,330 --> 00:14:57,170
[giggles]

332
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:59,290
♪

333
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:00,290
[grunts]

334
00:15:01,670 --> 00:15:02,830
Huh?

335
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:04,460
What are you...

336
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:06,750
Did Gladus tell you anything?

337
00:15:06,830 --> 00:15:07,670
[ANNE]
What?

338
00:15:07,750 --> 00:15:09,670
I'm sorry. I don't know.

339
00:15:09,750 --> 00:15:10,750
Did he?

340
00:15:10,830 --> 00:15:14,460
He said that I smell
like silver sugar but...

341
00:15:16,170 --> 00:15:17,580
[sighs]

342
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:19,920
[ANNE]
Challe?

343
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,630
[gasps]

344
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,290
Challe, I--

345
00:15:36,380 --> 00:15:38,040
You're far too trusting.

346
00:15:38,130 --> 00:15:40,330
Are you saying
that he's dangerous?

347
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:41,460
Perhaps.

348
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:43,080
So don't let your guard down.

349
00:15:43,170 --> 00:15:44,040
Right.

350
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:46,750
[gasps]

351
00:15:46,830 --> 00:15:48,880
- Good girl.
- [gasps]

352
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:54,330
You couldn't sleep last night.

353
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:55,960
You'd better stay in my room.

354
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:57,580
Mmm-hmm.

355
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,960
I'll keep watch over Noah.

356
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:02,330
Go on.

357
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,130
[ANNE]
Thank you!

358
00:16:05,540 --> 00:16:07,460
[crickets chirp]

359
00:16:10,750 --> 00:16:11,960
[sighs]

360
00:16:16,630 --> 00:16:18,250
[sighs]

361
00:16:19,250 --> 00:16:22,080
[ANNE] He's protecting me
as though I'm a child.

362
00:16:22,170 --> 00:16:24,000
But still,

363
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,710
I'm so happy.

364
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:31,710
[HERBERT]
Young Silver Sugar Master.

365
00:16:32,250 --> 00:16:33,710
Huh?

366
00:16:35,630 --> 00:16:37,210
[ANNE]
Am I dreaming?

367
00:16:37,290 --> 00:16:38,130
Oh!

368
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,830
[NOAH]
Lord Herbert, it's your turn.

369
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,170
Huh?

370
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:48,000
[HERBERT]
Hmm.

371
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:53,380
Should I move here?

372
00:16:54,130 --> 00:16:56,080
[NOAH]
Why's it taking you so long?

373
00:16:56,170 --> 00:16:57,790
[ANNE]
Who is that?

374
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,290
Is he Noah's master?

375
00:17:08,170 --> 00:17:09,790
Here, try one of these, Noah.

376
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:11,290
Would you?

377
00:17:15,290 --> 00:17:17,580
That crest is such
a beautiful detail.

378
00:17:18,170 --> 00:17:21,290
That's because it stands
for the pride of my family.

379
00:17:21,710 --> 00:17:24,630
The lion, swords, and shield are
symbols of strength

380
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:26,630
and the blue flag
for compassion.

381
00:17:26,710 --> 00:17:27,960
Its full meaning is,

382
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:29,750
"Follow me,
for I use my strength

383
00:17:29,830 --> 00:17:30,960
to care for the people."

384
00:17:31,670 --> 00:17:35,290
Even so, I don't know a thing
about wielding a sword.

385
00:17:35,790 --> 00:17:36,630
Perhaps,

386
00:17:36,710 --> 00:17:39,080
but you have a strong heart
instead Lord Herbert,

387
00:17:39,170 --> 00:17:41,420
and you're extremely kind.

388
00:17:42,630 --> 00:17:44,540
Forgive me for asking, sir

389
00:17:44,630 --> 00:17:47,670
but why do you keep me here
when I'm so useless?

390
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:49,170
Don't be absurd!

391
00:17:49,250 --> 00:17:50,460
You're far from useless.

392
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:51,750
[NOAH]
That isn't true!

393
00:17:51,830 --> 00:17:54,630
I'm clumsy
and I'm always breaking dishes.

394
00:17:54,710 --> 00:17:56,880
I've never been
of any help to you.

395
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:58,460
You help me quite often.

396
00:17:58,540 --> 00:18:00,130
For example,

397
00:18:00,210 --> 00:18:02,670
you are the only one who is
an equal opponent for me

398
00:18:02,750 --> 00:18:04,210
when I'm playing a game.

399
00:18:04,290 --> 00:18:05,830
You're just as bad at them
as I am,

400
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,420
it's much more fun that way.

401
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:09,670
Well, that may be true sir,

402
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:12,170
but I wouldn't really
consider it a compliment.

403
00:18:12,250 --> 00:18:14,250
[HERBERT]
Well, perhaps you should.

404
00:18:14,330 --> 00:18:17,460
[NOAH, HERBERT]
[laugh]

405
00:18:19,580 --> 00:18:21,170
[thunder rumbles]

406
00:18:21,250 --> 00:18:23,330
How can you just go off
and leave me!

407
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:26,540
Lord Herbert, please answer me!

408
00:18:26,630 --> 00:18:27,750
[HERBERT]
I told you.

409
00:18:27,830 --> 00:18:29,420
Until I can return home,

410
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:31,960
I need you to look after
the castle for me.

411
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:33,670
[NOAH]
Why me!

412
00:18:35,670 --> 00:18:37,330
Anyone else could stay.

413
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,210
[HERBERT]
Here.

414
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:43,040
- Take these.
- [gasps]

415
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:46,670
I want you to eat them.

416
00:18:47,210 --> 00:18:48,040
Huh?

417
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:03,710
If they found these,
they'd crush them to bits,

418
00:19:03,790 --> 00:19:06,880
so I'd much rather have you
eat them instead.

419
00:19:08,710 --> 00:19:11,540
Noah, please protect this place.

420
00:19:11,630 --> 00:19:15,250
It's an important task
that only you can fulfil for me.

421
00:19:15,710 --> 00:19:17,330
But listen,

422
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:18,830
don't eat anything else here

423
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:21,210
besides the confections
I just gave you.

424
00:19:21,290 --> 00:19:22,670
Huh?

425
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:26,960
When you get hungry
and feel like eating something,

426
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:29,500
I would like for you to leave,
all right?

427
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:30,500
But why?

428
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:33,420
[NOAH gasps]

429
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,500
I don't understand at all!

430
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,540
Tell me.

431
00:19:39,210 --> 00:19:42,750
[thunder rumbles]

432
00:19:46,710 --> 00:19:48,710
[NOAH]
Then I won't eat these.

433
00:19:48,790 --> 00:19:51,040
[sobs]

434
00:19:51,130 --> 00:19:52,420
I refuse to.

435
00:19:56,420 --> 00:19:57,920
[ANNE]
Noah...

436
00:20:01,250 --> 00:20:02,670
[HERBERT]
I have a request of you,

437
00:20:02,750 --> 00:20:05,380
young Silver Sugar Master.

438
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:07,830
Please find a way to save him.

439
00:20:08,830 --> 00:20:10,290
[grunts]

440
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:15,210
What should I do?

441
00:20:15,290 --> 00:20:16,540
Huh?

442
00:20:16,630 --> 00:20:18,630
[rain patters]

443
00:20:24,290 --> 00:20:25,580
It's raining?

444
00:20:25,670 --> 00:20:26,960
At this time of year?

445
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:29,130
- [KING] In here! Quick!
- Huh?

446
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,330
[ORLAND]
The silver sugar!

447
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:35,000
[ANNE gasps]

448
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:36,540
It hardened!

449
00:20:36,630 --> 00:20:37,710
What do we do now!

450
00:20:37,790 --> 00:20:39,790
[VALENTINE]
This is completely solid!

451
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:41,170
[ORLAND]
These are, too.

452
00:20:41,250 --> 00:20:43,460
[KING] They've absorbed
the humidity, as well.

453
00:20:43,540 --> 00:20:45,130
[grunts] Check them all!

454
00:20:45,210 --> 00:20:46,880
See what we can salvage!

455
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:48,130
Move them over there!

456
00:20:48,210 --> 00:20:49,460
- [VALENTINE] Right!
- [NADIR] We're too late!

457
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:51,170
- The rain soaked through!
- [ORLAND] It's ruined.

458
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,750
[ELLIOTT] Blast it!
Every one of them is drenched!

459
00:20:53,830 --> 00:20:56,210
- Oh, no! -This barrel is...
- This too.

460
00:20:56,290 --> 00:20:57,790
How can this be?

